profile: tinyrustlm.short-term-memory.v8
updated_utc: 2026-07-02T20:30:00Z
current_package_version: 1.5.0
current_goal: TinyRustLM.MiRust.com is the TinyRustLM developer portal; TinyRustLM.com is the root browser-local app; Runtime.MiRust.com content is preserved under docs/runtime-portal/ and no longer acts as a separate documentation authority.
latest_changes:
  - Documented MiniModel known-peer `serve-peer-pieces` / `fetch-peer-pieces` handoffs in the developer portal while keeping broad discovery/relay as later work.
  - Added /developer-portal/ route.
  - Preserved Runtime.MiRust.com docs, reports, package metadata, page registry, llms exports, sitemap, version marker, and health marker under docs/runtime-portal/.
  - Added docs/runtime-portal/MANIFEST.md with byte counts and SHA-256 checksums.
  - Updated docs/long-term-memory.md and .uai/long-term-memory.uai pointer records.
  - Updated llms.txt, llms-full.txt, sitemap.xml, workspace.uai, and public talisman boundaries.
  - Added proof-ready MiniModel catalog-entry language: catalog metadata is based on admitted manifests plus `.minimodel-peer-offer` proof and optional `peer_source_count`/`peer_sources`; `prepare-peer-share` is the normal sender path, and TinyRustLM shows P2P Import only when a catalog-listed or saved consenting peer source exists.
  - Updated Known peer URL behavior: TinyRustLM now records one list-level consenting direct `http://` peer URL as the fallback for proof-ready rows without catalog peer sources, rejects project/Hugging Face hosts as peer sources, and writes that URL into the generated peer-import JSON/script.
  - Updated P2P receiver behavior: generated peer-import scripts now call MiniModel `import-peer-request <request-json> <manifest> <output-dir>` so Rust validates the request, fetches, assembles, verifies, and writes the receipt through one command.
  - Updated Hugging Face conversion docs: TinyRustLM's Start Conversion handoff now runs local Rust conversion/validation and then MiniModel `prepare-peer-share`, which writes the manifest, peer-offer proof, local piece set, and metadata-only catalog entry in one command.
next_read:
  - /developer-portal/
  - .uai/long-term-memory.uai
  - docs/runtime-portal/MANIFEST.md
  - docs/report-index.md
  - docs/long-term-memory.md
